<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_LREALFromEPICS" Id="{1404ab4d-b135-464e-bd7c-11d3ea997668}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
Function block to link an analog value from EPICS to an LREAL on the PLC

Purpose:

    Receive one floating-point value from an EPICS link record (created by the
    pytmc pragma shown under Usage) and hold it in `.fValue` for use by PLC
    control logic, together with a `.bValid` flag that reports whether EPICS is
    still writing values and whether the link is still within the accepted
    severity. This block owns the IOC heartbeat/timeout handling and the
    link-severity check, so no caller has to re-implement them.

Usage:

    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: INTERNAL:RECORD
        link: PV:NAME:TO:LINK:TO
    '}
    fbLinkedValue1 : FB_LREALFromEPICS;

Such that when PV:NAME:TO:LINK:TO changes in EPICS, the INTERNAL:RECORD will be used to
push a value through to the PLC with this function block.

As this block takes care of IOC heartbeat signals and monitors the link and value severity,
the end-user should then only have to look at `.bValid` and `.fValue`. These are guaranteed to
be up-to-date and valid within `tTimeout` seconds.

Call the instance once per PLC cycle and treat `.fValue` as usable only while
`.bValid` is TRUE:

    fbLinkedValue1();
    IF fbLinkedValue1.bValid THEN
        fPressure := fbLinkedValue1.fValue;  // engineering units of the link PV
    END_IF

Objectives:

    - Give the analog data path from EPICS one block that owns the timeout and
      link-severity handling, so control logic consumes one value plus one
      validity flag instead of repeating those checks at every call site.
    - Never let a stale or alarming link reach control logic unnoticed: `.bValid`
      drops when EPICS stops writing for `tTimeout`, and when the reported link
      severity is worse than `iMaximumValidSeverity`.
    - Keep the last good value available in `.fValue` while the link is not
      valid, so a caller can hold its last commanded state rather than act on
      an invalid sample.

History:

    2020-02-26  K Lauer: created the function block (afb0619).
    2020-08-31  K Lauer: added the `iMaximumValidSeverity` input and relaxed the
                validity test from `iLastValidSeverity = 0` (NO_ALARM only) to
                `iLastValidSeverity <= iMaximumValidSeverity` (5514329).
    2021-11-02  K Lauer: style pass, re-formatted by pre-commit (567ce06).
    2023-05-22  Jakob Sagatowski: dropped the ProductVersion attribute from the
                .TcPOU XML header, no code change (2766f0d).
    2026-11-27  Scirix Agent: added the purpose/objectives/history/author
                sections and commented every declaration; comment only, no
                behaviour change (audit finding #1074, convention
                conv_321640e095c0).

Author/Date:

    2020-02-26  K Lauer
*)

FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_LREALFromEPICS

VAR_INPUT
    // Highest EPICS link severity that still counts as a healthy link for
    // `.bValid`. EPICS severity codes: 0 = NO_ALARM, 1 = MINOR, 2 = MAJOR,
    // 3 = INVALID. Range: 0..3 [-]. The default 1 accepts NO_ALARM and MINOR
    // and lets `.bValid` drop as soon as the link goes MAJOR or INVALID (for
    // example because the IOC stopped or the link PV is disconnected).
    iMaximumValidSeverity		: INT := 1;
END_VAR

VAR_OUTPUT
    // TRUE while `.fValue` may be used by control logic: the last link
    // severity reported by EPICS is <= `iMaximumValidSeverity` AND both the
    // value and the severity have been refreshed within `tTimeout` (2 s).
    // FALSE means `.fValue` is stale (EPICS silent) or the link is alarming:
    // hold the last commanded state instead of acting on the value.
    // Note: both TON timers start with Q = FALSE, so `.bValid` reads TRUE from
    // the first cycle until `tTimeout` after the first write, i.e. before any
    // sample has actually arrived.
    bValid				: BOOL;
    // The last value received from EPICS, in the engineering units of the
    // linked PV: this block applies no scaling, offset or unit conversion, so
    // the unit [-] is whatever the IOC publishes for PV:NAME:TO:LINK:TO.
    // Holds the last good value and is not zeroed when `.bValid` goes FALSE.
    fValue				: LREAL;
END_VAR

VAR
    // Alias of `fPLCInternalValue` viewed as a raw 64-bit pattern, so the
    // IEEE-754 NaN sentinel `NAN_VALUE` can be compared bit-for-bit instead of
    // numerically (any numeric comparison against NaN is false). ADR() is
    // taken every cycle, so the alias always follows the same variable.
    iValueInvalidate	: POINTER TO ULINT;
    // Off-delay timer restarted on every new value written by EPICS: Q goes
    // TRUE `tTimeout` (2 s) after the last write, i.e. the value has gone
    // stale. Q is one of the three terms of `.bValid`.
    tonValueTimeout		: TON;
    // Same off-delay timer for the link severity: restarted on every new
    // severity reported by EPICS, Q TRUE means no severity update within
    // `tTimeout`. Q is one of the three terms of `.bValid`.
    tonSeverityTimeout	: TON;

    // Last value received from EPICS, buffered so `.fValue` keeps the last
    // good reading while `.bValid` is FALSE. Units: those of the linked PV
    // (no scaling is applied by this block).
    fLastValidValue 	: LREAL;
    // Last link severity received from EPICS (EPICS code: 0 = NO_ALARM,
    // 1 = MINOR, 2 = MAJOR, 3 = INVALID), compared against
    // `iMaximumValidSeverity` to form `.bValid`. Initial 0 = NO_ALARM, so the
    // first cycle latches NO_ALARM and starts `tonSeverityTimeout`.
    iLastValidSeverity 	: INT;

    // EPICS-written copy of the linked PV value. The pytmc pragma below
    // creates the 'EPICSLink' record whose link pushes the PV's value in
    // here; this block reads it and writes `NAN_VALUE` back once consumed.
    // Units: those of the linked PV [-].
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: EPICSLink
        link:
        field: DESC Internal variable used to monitor EPICS PV in PLC
    '}
    fPLCInternalValue : LREAL;

    // EPICS-written copy of the linked PV's alarm severity (SEVR), linked
    // through the pragma below ('*EPICSLink.SEVR'). -1 is the 'nothing new'
    // sentinel that this block writes back after latching a severity; any
    // other value is a fresh EPICS severity code (0 = NO_ALARM, 1 = MINOR,
    // 2 = MAJOR, 3 = INVALID) [-].
    // Use special link syntax for now to get EPICSLink.SEVR here:
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: EPICSLink:LinkSeverity
        link: *EPICSLink.SEVR
        field: DESC Internal variable used to monitor EPICS PV severity in PLC
    '}
    iPLCInternalSeverity : INT;

END_VAR
VAR CONSTANT
    // Staleness limit for the link [TIME, 2 s]: both the value and the link
    // severity must be refreshed by EPICS within this period, otherwise
    // `.bValid` goes FALSE when `tonValueTimeout` / `tonSeverityTimeout` expire.
    tTimeout			: TIME := T#2S;
    // 'No new value yet' sentinel that this block writes into
    // `fPLCInternalValue` after it consumes a sample: the IEEE-754 NaN bit
    // pattern 0x7FFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF. EPICS overwrites it with the linked PV's
    // value when it pushes a new sample, so a pattern other than `NAN_VALUE`
    // means 'fresh value'. The comparison is done on the raw 64-bit pattern
    // through `iValueInvalidate` because a NaN never compares equal
    // numerically [-].
    NAN_VALUE   		: ULINT := 16#7f_ff_ff_ff__ff_ff_ff_ff;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[iValueInvalidate := ADR(fPLCInternalValue);

IF iPLCInternalSeverity <> -1 THEN
    // New severity value
    iLastValidSeverity := iPLCInternalSeverity;
    iPLCInternalSeverity := -1;

     // Reset the timer
    tonSeverityTimeout(IN:=FALSE);
    tonSeverityTimeout(IN:=TRUE, PT:=tTimeout);
END_IF

IF iValueInvalidate^ <> NAN_VALUE THEN
    // New value from EPICS
    fLastValidValue 	:= fPLCInternalValue;
    iValueInvalidate^	:= NAN_VALUE;

    // Reset the timer
    tonValueTimeout(IN:=FALSE);
    tonValueTimeout(IN:=TRUE, PT:=tTimeout);
END_IF

tonValueTimeout();
tonSeverityTimeout();
bValid := (NOT tonValueTimeout.Q) AND
          (NOT tonSeverityTimeout.Q) AND
          (iLastValidSeverity <= iMaximumValidSeverity);
fValue := fLastValidValue;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>